       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\n- **Order as written:** acetaminophen 2000 mg PO three times daily is 6,000 mg/day.\n- **Daily limit:** the usual maximum for a healthy adult is 4,000 mg/day. Many institutions use 3,000 mg/day. 6,000 mg/day carries a real risk of hepatotoxicity, even with normal liver function.\n- **Single dose:** the usual maximum is 1,000 mg, so 2,000 mg is also above that.\n\nHere are some options that may be what you meant:\n1. **Acetaminophen 1000 mg PO three times daily.** This is 3,000 mg/day.\n2. **Acetaminophen 1000 mg PO four times daily.** This is 4,000 mg/day, the maximum.\n3. **Acetaminophen 650 mg PO every 6 hours.** This is 2,600 mg/day.\n\nIf you do want 2000 mg three times daily, please confirm that it's intentional and give the clinical rationale. I'd still be hesitant to enter it, and it may need pharmacy review first.\n\nTell me which option you want and I'll enter it right away."
